@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `nii-il34-nouns`
IMPORT `nii-s336-s340-s343`

-- TESTS for ss 336, 340, 340A and 343 (row IL-34). Expected values worked by hand from the Hebrew; the arithmetic is beside each group.
-- The average wage 13,566 is the consolidation's own note on s 1 ("in 2026, 13,566"); half of it is 6,783.

§ `Tests: sections 336, 340, 340A and 343`

§§ `Section 336: the end of the payment period`

#ASSERT `s 336 — the last day of the payment period holding the day` (YMD 2026 2 10) `, other limits having been set being` FALSE EQUALS YMD 2026 2 28
#ASSERT `s 336 — the last day of the payment period holding the day` (YMD 2028 2 10) `, other limits having been set being` FALSE EQUALS YMD 2028 2 29
#ASSERT `s 336 — the last day of the payment period holding the day` (YMD 2026 12 31) `, other limits having been set being` FALSE EQUALS YMD 2026 12 31
#ASSERT `s 336 — the last day of the payment period holding the day` (YMD 2026 4 1) `, other limits having been set being` FALSE EQUALS YMD 2026 4 30
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 336 — the last day of the payment period holding the day` (YMD 2026 2 10) `, other limits having been set being` TRUE BECAUSE "an order of the Minister under section 336 sets other limits for this payment period, and it is not deposited"

§§ `The temporary figures: which years`

#ASSERT REFUSED `the temporary figures apply in the year` 2024 `, an order extending the temporary period being` FALSE BECAUSE "this provision was added by Amendment No. 252 from 1 January 2025 and did not exist before"
#ASSERT     `the temporary figures apply in the year` 2025 `, an order extending the temporary period being` FALSE
#ASSERT     `the temporary figures apply in the year` 2026 `, an order extending the temporary period being` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `the temporary figures apply in the year` 2027 `, an order extending the temporary period being` FALSE
#ASSERT     `the temporary figures apply in the year` 2027 `, an order extending the temporary period being` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `the temporary figures apply in the year` 2028 `, an order extending the temporary period being` FALSE
#ASSERT     `the temporary figures apply in the year` 2028 `, an order extending the temporary period being` TRUE
-- Amendment 252 s 7(b) reaches 2027 and 2028 only: an order "for 2029" extends nothing.
#ASSERT NOT `the temporary figures apply in the year` 2029 `, an order extending the temporary period being` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `the temporary figures apply in the year` 2030 `, an order extending the temporary period being` FALSE

§§ `Section 340(a)(2) and (c)`

#ASSERT     `s 340(a)(2) — the rate fixed for another insured person is valid: fixed` 0.5 `, the item 4 rate` (JUST 0.78)
#ASSERT     `s 340(a)(2) — the rate fixed for another insured person is valid: fixed` 0.78 `, the item 4 rate` (JUST 0.78)
#ASSERT NOT `s 340(a)(2) — the rate fixed for another insured person is valid: fixed` 0.8 `, the item 4 rate` (JUST 0.78)
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 340(a)(2) — the rate fixed for another insured person is valid: fixed` 0.1 `, the item 4 rate` NOTHING BECAUSE "Schedule J item 4 prints no rate (a dash) for an insured person who is neither an employee nor self-employed, so the ceiling of section 340(a)(2) is not a number"
-- 70% x 0.94 = 0.658 for a resident of the Area who is not an Israeli resident there; the item 1 rate otherwise.
#ASSERT `s 340(c) — the maternity insurance rate: item 1 rate` 0.94 `, a resident of the Area who is not an Israeli resident there being` TRUE EQUALS 0.658
#ASSERT `s 340(c) — the maternity insurance rate: item 1 rate` 0.94 `, a resident of the Area who is not an Israeli resident there being` FALSE EQUALS 0.94

§§ `Section 340(d) and (e)`

-- Half of 13,566 is 6,783. 0.53% x 6,783 = 35.9499 (2025 and 2026); 0.4% x 6,783 = 27.132 (2027 with no order, 2029).
#ASSERT `s 340(d) — the monthly work-injury contribution for training or rehabilitation, year` 2025 `, an order extending the temporary period being` FALSE `, the average wage being` 13_566 EQUALS 35.9499
#ASSERT `s 340(d) — the monthly work-injury contribution for training or rehabilitation, year` 2026 `, an order extending the temporary period being` FALSE `, the average wage being` 13_566 EQUALS 35.9499
#ASSERT `s 340(d) — the monthly work-injury contribution for training or rehabilitation, year` 2027 `, an order extending the temporary period being` FALSE `, the average wage being` 13_566 EQUALS 27.132
#ASSERT `s 340(d) — the monthly work-injury contribution for training or rehabilitation, year` 2027 `, an order extending the temporary period being` TRUE `, the average wage being` 13_566 EQUALS 35.9499
#ASSERT `s 340(d) — the monthly work-injury contribution for training or rehabilitation, year` 2029 `, an order extending the temporary period being` FALSE `, the average wage being` 13_566 EQUALS 27.132
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 340(d) — the monthly work-injury contribution for training or rehabilitation, year` 2024 `, an order extending the temporary period being` FALSE `, the average wage being` 13_566 BECAUSE "this provision was added by Amendment No. 252 from 1 January 2025 and did not exist before"
-- (e): 0.13% x 6,783 = 8.8179; 0.1% x 6,783 = 6.783.
#ASSERT `s 340(e) — the monthly maternity contribution for vocational training, year` 2026 `, an order extending the temporary period being` FALSE `, the average wage being` 13_566 EQUALS 8.8179
#ASSERT `s 340(e) — the monthly maternity contribution for vocational training, year` 2027 `, an order extending the temporary period being` FALSE `, the average wage being` 13_566 EQUALS 6.783
#ASSERT `s 340(e) — the monthly maternity contribution for vocational training, year` 2028 `, an order extending the temporary period being` TRUE `, the average wage being` 13_566 EQUALS 8.8179

§§ `Section 340A: a household worker`

-- A wage of 30,000 in the quarter. Insured under Chapter 11: 7.85% = 2,355 (2026); 6.25% = 1,875 (2027, no order). Not insured, or s 351(b) or (d): 3.6% = 1,080; 2% = 600.
#ASSERT `s 340A — the employer's contributions for a household worker for a quarter, year` 2026 `, an order extending the temporary period being` FALSE `, wage` 30_000 `, insured under Chapter 11 and not under section 351(b) or (d) being` TRUE EQUALS 2_355
#ASSERT `s 340A — the employer's contributions for a household worker for a quarter, year` 2027 `, an order extending the temporary period being` FALSE `, wage` 30_000 `, insured under Chapter 11 and not under section 351(b) or (d) being` TRUE EQUALS 1_875
#ASSERT `s 340A — the employer's contributions for a household worker for a quarter, year` 2027 `, an order extending the temporary period being` TRUE `, wage` 30_000 `, insured under Chapter 11 and not under section 351(b) or (d) being` TRUE EQUALS 2_355
#ASSERT `s 340A — the employer's contributions for a household worker for a quarter, year` 2026 `, an order extending the temporary period being` FALSE `, wage` 30_000 `, insured under Chapter 11 and not under section 351(b) or (d) being` FALSE EQUALS 1_080
#ASSERT `s 340A — the employer's contributions for a household worker for a quarter, year` 2027 `, an order extending the temporary period being` FALSE `, wage` 30_000 `, insured under Chapter 11 and not under section 351(b) or (d) being` FALSE EQUALS 600
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 340A — the employer's contributions for a household worker for a quarter, year` 2024 `, an order extending the temporary period being` FALSE `, wage` 30_000 `, insured under Chapter 11 and not under section 351(b) or (d) being` TRUE BECAUSE "this provision was added by Amendment No. 252 from 1 January 2025 and did not exist before"
-- The deduction from the worker's wage: 1.8% x 30,000 = 540 (2026); 1% x 30,000 = 300 (2027, no order).
#ASSERT `s 340A(a)(2) — the most the employer may deduct from the worker's wage for a quarter, year` 2026 `, an order extending the temporary period being` FALSE `, wage` 30_000 EQUALS 540
#ASSERT `s 340A(a)(2) — the most the employer may deduct from the worker's wage for a quarter, year` 2027 `, an order extending the temporary period being` FALSE `, wage` 30_000 EQUALS 300
#ASSERT `s 340A(a)(2) — the most the employer may deduct from the worker's wage for a quarter, year` 2028 `, an order extending the temporary period being` TRUE `, wage` 30_000 EQUALS 540

§§ `Section 343: the employer the Minister may approve`

#ASSERT     `s 343 — the employer is one the Minister may approve` (`An employer's position under section 343` WITH `the number of employees` IS 500, `bound by law, a collective agreement or a contract to pay wages for the time injury allowance is paid` IS TRUE, `the total wages the employer pays for that time` IS 10_000, `the injury allowance paid for that time` IS 10_000)
#ASSERT NOT `s 343 — the employer is one the Minister may approve` (`An employer's position under section 343` WITH `the number of employees` IS 499, `bound by law, a collective agreement or a contract to pay wages for the time injury allowance is paid` IS TRUE, `the total wages the employer pays for that time` IS 10_000, `the injury allowance paid for that time` IS 10_000)
#ASSERT NOT `s 343 — the employer is one the Minister may approve` (`An employer's position under section 343` WITH `the number of employees` IS 500, `bound by law, a collective agreement or a contract to pay wages for the time injury allowance is paid` IS FALSE, `the total wages the employer pays for that time` IS 10_000, `the injury allowance paid for that time` IS 10_000)
#ASSERT NOT `s 343 — the employer is one the Minister may approve` (`An employer's position under section 343` WITH `the number of employees` IS 500, `bound by law, a collective agreement or a contract to pay wages for the time injury allowance is paid` IS TRUE, `the total wages the employer pays for that time` IS 9_999, `the injury allowance paid for that time` IS 10_000)
-- The reduced sum itself is the Minister's determination, which is not in the sources; an employer outside the conditions cannot be approved.
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 343 — the reduced contribution for an approved employer` (`An employer's position under section 343` WITH `the number of employees` IS 600, `bound by law, a collective agreement or a contract to pay wages for the time injury allowance is paid` IS TRUE, `the total wages the employer pays for that time` IS 12_000, `the injury allowance paid for that time` IS 10_000) BECAUSE "the reduced contributions the Minister determined under section 343 are not in the sources"
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 343 — the reduced contribution for an approved employer` (`An employer's position under section 343` WITH `the number of employees` IS 100, `bound by law, a collective agreement or a contract to pay wages for the time injury allowance is paid` IS TRUE, `the total wages the employer pays for that time` IS 12_000, `the injury allowance paid for that time` IS 10_000) BECAUSE "the employer does not meet the conditions of section 343 and cannot be approved for reduced contributions"
